fact WorkItem(id: "WI-622", description: some(value: "rule-body dot obligations should be relational-aware (float vs definite), generalizing WI-602 beyond value-preconditions. WI-602 made value-preconditions refutation-aware in rule-body dot dispatch and inverted dispatch_dots_in_occ to surface ALL type_check_node errors except DotDispatchNoMatch{receiver_sort:None} (removing a blanket Err(_) silent-skip). WI-557 premise: a rule body is relational, so op-body call-site obligations do not apply to symbolic rule-body vars. That premise is BROADER than value-preconditions: two OTHER op-body-only obligations now surface as potentially-SPURIOUS hard load errors for a rule-body value-method-dot. (1) spec-op DispatchNoMatch -- an abstract-spec-op dot (?x.compare(?y)) cannot be licensed because the rule-body env has empty op_requires (an op body requires Ordered[T] licenses it). (2) UnconstrainedTypeParam -- dispatch_dots_in_occ types the dot with expected=None, so an op whose type-param appears ONLY in its return type cannot be pinned (an op-body call site supplies expected via a let-annotation / return position), though it would resolve by unification at resolution time. Lower-confidence third case: argument-conformance TypeMismatch when a rule var infers to reflect Term (the pair.anthill self-typed-access weakness). UNREACHABLE today (no value-method-dot exists in any rule body in stdlib/tests -- suite is green), LATENT for future user programs. FIX TEMPLATE (per WI-602): make each obligation relational-aware -- definite violation raises, a float defers to runtime value-directed dispatch -- rather than an unconditional hard-error. Discovered by the WI-602 /code-review (3 finder angles converged on dispatch_dots_in_occ)."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: ["WI-602"]), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-07-06T06:28:26Z"))

fact Tag(workitem: "WI-622", name: "typing")
